		<ANNOTATION>
			<ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a155" TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts308" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts309">
				<ANNOTATION_VALUE>No, I think Cleaney thought very highly of Krezel He did but then the things that Kreisel did a number of them were close to things that Claimy was working on so there was a commonality of interest which wasn't the case with Kreisel and Tarski But that's getting off the Yeah no I'm just trying to get How is it that somebody can do mathematics and not be precise in that way?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
