			<ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a156" TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts310" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts311">
				<ANNOTATION_VALUE>Well no was I'm just trying to get more at what it was what the kind of thinking he did was and how far it transferred into say the kind of thinking you have to do for philosophy or for any kind of science was his method of attack sequence clarity that sequence is important and in a way it's like telling a story in a classical way or describing a life in a classical way you have to tell one thing before the next thing can be understood but also spelling everything out giving all the background that yeah there's no part of the picture that's left no part of the picture ambiguous vague yeah yeah And you can take something left to the imagination huh?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
